   "title": "<div style=\"display:table-cell\">\r\n<h3 style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px\">Question 11 (5 marks)</h3>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display:table-cell;padding-left:1rem\"><button class=\"hsc-tooltip nsw-button nsw-button--light\" style=\"padding:0.2rem;min-width:auto;\">Annotations<br />\r\n<span class=\"hsc-tooltiptext\">&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;Students will have the opportunity to create or modify spreadsheets using an actual application. Press INFO at the top right corner for the spreadsheet user guide.<br />\r\n&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;Decision Support Systems is mandatory content in the Enterprise Computing course. </span></button></div>\r\n",
   "layout": "3",
   "stimulus": "<style type=\"text/css\">.hsc-table-normal {\r\nborder-spacing: 0px;\r\nborder-collapse: collapse;\r\nmargin:10px 0px;\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\ntable.hsc-table-normal thead tr:first-child th {\r\ntext-align:left;\r\nfont-weight:bold;\r\nborder-collapse: collapse;\r\nborder-right: 1px solid currentColor !important;\r\nborder-left: 1px solid currentColor !important;\r\nborder-top: 1px solid currentColor !important;\r\nbackground-color: rgba(95, 204, 245, 0.3) !important;\r\npadding:3px 6px;\r\ncolor:currentColor;\r\n}\r\n\r\ntable.hsc-table-normal tbody tr:first-child td {\r\nborder: 1px solid currentColor !important;\r\nborder-collapse: collapse;\r\npadding:3px 6px;\r\nbackground-color:transparent !important;\r\ncolor:currentColor;\r\n}\r\ntable.hsc-table-normal tbody tr td {\r\nborder: 1px solid currentColor !important;\r\nborder-collapse: collapse;\r\npadding:3px 6px;\r\nbackground-color:transparent !important;\r\ncolor:currentColor;\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<p>A business wants to use a spreadsheet to create a decision support system that will streamline its staff hiring process. The business&rsquo;s hiring decisions are based on three scores achieved by each job applicant. A higher score indicates a more suitable applicant.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>The travelling score</strong><br />\r\nIf an applicant can travel to work within a specified time they score 10 points. If not, they score 0 points. The specified time should be given as data in the spreadsheet, so that it can be changed according to future circumstances.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>The experience score</strong><br />\r\nApplicants score points depending on the number of years they have worked. The table shows how points are allocated based on the number of years worked.</p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"margin:1rem 0px 0px 0px\">\r\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"hsc-table-normal\">\r\n\t<thead>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n   <th>Number of years worked</th>\r\n\t\t\t<th>Points</th>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</thead>\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0 year</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1&ndash;4 years</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>10</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>5&ndash;9 years</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>20</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>10 or more years</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>30</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>The interview score</strong><br />\r\nEach job applicant is interviewed and given a score out of 100.</p>\r\n",
